# vvaharness/agentdoc.py

Packaged operating instructions for AI coding agents. `vvaharness setup --install-agents` writes them into the files each agent reads (AGENTS.md and .github/copilot-instructions.md always; CLAUDE.md and a Claude skill only when `claude` is on PATH; GEMINI.md only when `gemini` is). Existing files are never overwritten. These are instructions to an outside agent that drives the tool, not prompts the harness sends.

Source: `vvaharness/agentdoc.py` (lines 1-106)
Executor: model (read by an external coding agent; the harness only writes the text)
Called from: `vvaharness/cli/_setup.py` (`--install-agents`)

// prompt-src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:26-91
AGENT_DOC {
  title: "Operating vvaharness (for AI coding agents)"
  Constraints {
    "`vvaharness` is a **released** CLI security-scanning product. **Operate it, do not develop or repair it.**"
    findings are triage candidates, not confirmed vulnerabilities
    // The four rules, quoted:
    "**Never edit the `vvaharness` package source** to make a scan run."
    "**Never hand-write config files.** Use a shipped profile via `--config`. The one sanctioned exception is a git-ignored `config.local.yaml` overlay."
    "**On any failure, run `vvaharness setup` (or `doctor`), fix the environment it points to, and re-run.**"
    "**Scan only code the user is authorized to scan. Never arm exploit verification or fix mode unless the user asks.**"
    run `vvaharness estimate --repo <path>` first (no spend), because prompts send target source to the provider and scans spend real tokens
    run `vvaharness setup`, then `vvaharness scan --repo <path> --stop-after s9` for detection only
    keep `--stop-after s9` to explicitly skip Stages 10 and 11 with any profile, even with `--remediate`
    to send no exploit verification traffic, "unset `EV_API_COLLECTION` and start a fresh run without `--resume`"
    behind a gateway with a JWT-shaped key, set ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL (and SSL_CERT_FILE for a private certificate authority)
    on failure: read the one-line message, run `vvaharness doctor`, fix what it flags, re-run; full trace with VVAHARNESS_DEBUG=1
  }
  // abstracted: agentdoc.py:53-86 (install commands, profile names default/sdk/full/taint/semgrep, which profiles enable Stages 10 and 11, exploit verification description) summarized above
}

// src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:94-102
CLAUDE_SKILL = frontmatter { name: "vvaharness", description: "Operate the vvaharness SAST CLI (install, setup, doctor, scan). Use when asked to scan a repo for vulnerabilities with vvaharness. Operate the tool; never edit its source or hand-write its config. Exploit verification is Beta and API-only; do not arm it unless asked." } + AGENT_DOC
// src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:105-106
fn gemini_doc():executor=code { return AGENT_DOC with "(for AI coding agents)" replaced by "(for the Gemini CLI)" }
